<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later -->
<Project>

  <!--
    Shared MSBuild properties for the CollectivePlatform packages. This repo is the one place
    the common platform abstractions live; the product repos consume the published packages
    instead of copy-porting these types.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>

    <!-- Package metadata (FOSS). No monetization or identity. -->
    <Authors>CollectivePlatform contributors</Authors>
    <Product>CollectivePlatform</Product>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>GPL-3.0-or-later</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <Copyright>Copyright (C) CollectivePlatform contributors</Copyright>

    <!-- Single source of truth for the package version. -->
    <!-- 1.1.0: Collective.Platform.Controls now ships the shared design system (Themes/Tokens.axaml
         + Themes/Controls.axaml) consumed by every desktop head.
         1.2.0: Controls adds the shared ConfirmDialog (yes/no destructive-action prompt) so heads
         stop hand-rolling inline confirm modals. Controls-only change; consumers can vendor just the
         new Collective.Platform.Controls.1.2.0.nupkg (it depends only on Avalonia).
         1.3.0: calm-minimal design pass — Border.card is now borderless (+ new Border.card-outlined
         escape hatch), section-header gains letter-spacing, and shared ListBox/ListBoxItem styles add
         roomy rounded rows with a soft selection. Propagates GIT's calm look to all heads.
         1.3.1: revert the borderless Border.card (user feedback) back to a bordered, rounded surface
         card so sections read as distinct cards; drop the now-redundant card-outlined. The other
         calm bits (quiet section-header, roomy lists) stay.
         1.4.0: Collective.Platform.Controls adds the shared Window module — WindowStateService
         (correct off-screen guard + maximized-preserves + off-UI-thread persist) over a dedicated
         "window" geometry blob, ThemeController (mode->ThemeVariant + apply + re-theme hook), and a
         shared AboutDialog. Controls now depends on Collective.Platform.Abstractions.
         1.4.1: WindowStateService adds a block-safe Load() + synchronous Apply(window, geometry) split
         so startup callers apply geometry on the UI thread without an await-on-UI-context deadlock risk
         (ApplyAsync retained for callers on a running message pump). This release also MERGES IN the
         parallel shared-UI-mechanics line (previously developed as a divergent 1.3.0): a command
         system (CollectiveCommand / CommandRegistry / CommandMatcher / KeymapModel feeding
         CommandPalette + CommandMenu + KeymapBehavior), a ToastService/ToastHost transient-notification
         surface, a FindBarModel/FindBar incremental find bar, and Collective.Platform.Secrets'
         EncryptedFileSecretStore. The Window module's AboutDialog (AboutDialogModel-based) is the
         canonical one; the parallel line's string-arg About was superseded by it.
         1.5.0: Secrets: shared DeviceKeyCipher/DeviceKeyProvider (consolidates Auth/SSH/Wiki copies),
         SealedCredentialStore (device-key-sealed id->secret map over ISettingsStore), and
         PosixFileSecretStore (permissions-only ~/.ssh-model alternative). SecretStores.CreateDefault
         picks DPAPI on Windows and the encrypted-at-rest EncryptedFileSecretStore on Linux/macOS
         (strictly stronger than the plaintext PosixFileSecretStore, which stays available by choice).
         1.6.0: small-services batch: RecentItems(Store), CrashGuard, IdleLock, SaveChangesDialog,
         ShortcutsDialog. Collective.Platform adds RecentItems/RecentItemsList/RecentItemsStore (a
         shared MRU list over ISettingsStore), CrashGuard (last-resort unhandled-exception crash
         logger, byte-identical "<product>-crash.log" filenames), and IdleLock (TimeProvider-driven
         auto-lock timer). Collective.Platform.Controls adds SaveChangesDialog (3-way
         save/discard/cancel data-safety prompt, complements ConfirmDialog) and
         ShortcutItem/ShortcutsDialogModel/ShortcutsDialog (a grouped keyboard-shortcut reference
         dialog, code-built like AboutDialog).
         1.7.0: document-tabs module: TabList<T> + DocumentTabStrip. Collective.Platform.Controls
         adds TabList<T> (pure, UI-free tab mechanics — keyed open-or-activate, Wiki-style
         replace-active-slot navigation, veto/dispose close hooks, neighbor selection on close —
         the shared core behind Code's WorkspaceViewModel and Wiki's OpenTabsViewModel) and
         DocumentTabStrip (a code-built Avalonia strip rendering any ItemsSource via
         Title/IsDirty/ToolTip selectors, raising TabActivated/TabCloseRequested/NewTabRequested;
         no ICommand, delegate-driven like FolderBrowserDialog/AboutDialog). The tab/active Border
         styles ported from CollectiveWiki's hand-rolled strip onto the shared Collective.* tokens
         (Collective.Chrome / Collective.Surface / Collective.Accent).
         1.8.0: NEW Collective.Platform.Testing package (BCL-only deterministic test doubles —
         FakeFileSystem, FakeSettingsStore, ManualTimeProvider, TempDirectory, FakeDirectoryFileSystem —
         so repos stop copy-porting them) + the file-exploring module: the directory-aware seam
         IDirectoryFileSystem/DirectoryEntry (Abstractions) and the shared tree model
         PhysicalDirectoryFileSystem/FileTreeNode/FileTreeWalk/FileTreeFilter/PathTreeBuilder
         (Platform, BCL-only) — the canonical generalization of CollectiveCode's FileNode + Wiki's
         tree builder, provable on local disk and remote SFTP.
         1.8.1: FileTreeFilter dot handling is now split by kind — SkipDotFiles + SkipDotDirectories
         (replacing SkipDotEntries) — so a code file tree can show dot-files (.gitignore/.env) while
         still hiding dot-directories (.git/.vscode). Default behaviour is unchanged (both hidden).
         1.9.0: file-explorer UI pass. Collective.Platform adds FileSystemOperations (BCL-only disk
         mutation the file-exploring module lacked — create/rename/delete/copy/move, collision-suffixed,
         cross-volume-safe). Collective.Platform.Controls adds the shared FileExplorerControl (a
         code-built breadcrumb+list explorer over IDirectoryFileSystem — the alternative to the flat
         tree) plus its pure, unit-tested models ExplorerHistory / BreadcrumbTrail / FolderListing and
         FileIconFactory. Controls now references Collective.Platform (the control's AllowEdit path uses
         FileSystemOperations). Consumers vendoring Controls 1.9.0 also vendor Collective.Platform 1.9.0.
         Consumed by the new CollectiveFiles app and CollectiveCode's sidebar.
         1.9.1: folder-picker follow-up. Collective.Platform.Controls adds FolderPickerDialog — a
         folder chooser built on FileExplorerControl (breadcrumb + contents list, directories-only,
         read-only) with a "Select Folder" button and the same ShowAsync(owner, startPath) signature as
         FolderBrowserDialog, so it is a drop-in richer alternative. FileExplorerControl gains
         DirectoriesOnly (folder-picker mode) and hides its New File/Folder buttons when AllowEdit is
         off. First adopted by CollectiveWiki's "open vault" flow.
         1.10.0: crash-logging hardening + file-explorer bug fix. Collective.Platform's CrashGuard now
         APPENDS each crash (was overwrite) with a per-entry environment header (app version, OS+arch,
         .NET runtime) and a 512 KB soft cap; FormatEntry is a pure helper. Collective.Platform.Controls
         fixes FileExplorerControl.BuildRow throwing NullReferenceException when Avalonia re-invokes the
         row template with a null item during virtualization clear/recycle (crashed CollectiveFiles, and
         CollectiveWiki via its Open-Vault FolderPickerDialog). Re-vendored into CollectiveWiki +
         CollectiveFiles.
         1.11.0: utility-window chrome foundation. Collective.Platform.Controls adds UtilityWindow
         (base for every secondary window: token Collective.Surface background at style priority so
         local values win, owner->DefaultIcon icon inheritance on Opened, CenterOwner with a
         CenterScreen fallback when ownerless) and DialogWindow (modal prompts: Width 440/MinWidth 320,
         height-to-content, fixed-size, no taskbar entry, Escape closes when unhandled), plus
         DialogScaffold.Build/DialogButtons.Primary|Secondary|Danger helpers and a
         StackPanel.dialog-footer style. All shared dialogs (Confirm/SaveChanges/About/Shortcuts/
         FolderBrowser/FolderPicker) and CommandPalette re-base onto the new types - same public APIs.
         New Collective.Platform.Controls.Headless.Tests project (xunit.v3 + Avalonia.Headless.XUnit,
         isolated from the xunit-2.x Controls.Tests).
         1.12.0: DocumentTabStrip gains a per-tab right-click menu — Close / Close Others / Close to
         the Left / Close to the Right / Close All — raising the new TabCloseScopeRequested event
         (TabCloseScope enum + TabCloseScopeEventArgs carrying the anchor tab); items that would be
         no-ops for the clicked tab's position are greyed out. The ✕ button + middle-click and the
         existing TabActivated/TabCloseRequested/NewTabRequested events are unchanged (non-breaking).
         The scoped-close logic lives once in TabList<T> (CloseOthers/ToLeft/ToRight/AllAsync — guarded,
         a vetoed save aborts the batch), and DocumentTabStrip.Bind(list, title, …) wires items,
         selectors, activate, close, the scoped closes, active→selection sync and the + button in one
         call — so a head adopting document tabs doesn't re-hand-wire events and inherits future tab
         behaviour on re-vendor. Re-vendored into CollectiveWiki + CollectiveDocs (the two consumers). -->
    <Version>1.12.1</Version>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
